  "recipes": {
   "css": ".swap { display:grid; }\n.swap > * { grid-area:1/1; transition: opacity .6s cubic-bezier(.65,0,.35,1), filter .6s cubic-bezier(.65,0,.35,1); }\n.swap > :not(.on) { opacity:0; filter: blur(10px); }\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .swap > * { transition: opacity .2s linear; filter:none !important; } }",
   "waapi": "const opts = { duration: 600, easing: 'cubic-bezier(.65,0,.35,1)', fill: 'forwards' };\noldEl.animate([{ opacity: 1, filter: 'blur(0px)' }, { opacity: 0, filter: 'blur(10px)' }], opts);\nnewEl.animate([{ opacity: 0, filter: 'blur(10px)' }, { opacity: 1, filter: 'blur(0px)' }], opts);",
   "ae": "1. 두 텍스트 레이어를 같은 위치에 겹친다\n2. 이전 단어: 블러(가우스) 0 → 10, 불투명도 100 → 0%\n3. 새 단어: 블러 10 → 0, 불투명도 0 → 100%(같은 18프레임, 이지이즈)\n4. 액체처럼 만들려면 조정 레이어에 블러 + 레벨 보정(알파 입력 흑/백을 조인다)",
   "aeEn": "1. Stack two text layers in the same spot\n2. Old word: Gaussian Blur 0 → 10, Opacity 100 → 0%\n3. New word: Blur 10 → 0, Opacity 0 → 100% (same 18 frames, Easy Ease)\n4. For a liquid look, add an adjustment layer with Blur + Levels (tighten alpha input black/white)"
  },
